WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.307 --> 00:00:13.449
Hello! I'm Kat, and I'm a helicopter pilot.

2
00:00:14.729 --> 00:00:16.710
Today I have an important mission.

3
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.632
A man was hiking in the mountains and got hurt.

4
00:00:21.852 --> 00:00:24.893
I'm transporting rescue workers to the mountain to help him.

5
00:00:26.074 --> 00:00:28.295
Helicopters are great rescue vehicles.

6
00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:31.456
Climb aboard mine, and I'll tell you why.

7
00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:35.552
See that airplane?

8
00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:39.613
It needs a long airstrip to take off and land.

9
00:00:45.555 --> 00:00:47.116
Helicopters don't need that.

10
00:00:48.556 --> 00:00:50.677
They can lift straight up off the ground!

11
00:00:54.858 --> 00:00:57.939
And they can land in places where an airplane can't land.

12
00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:02.620
That makes them perfect for rescue missions like this one.

13
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.861
While we fly, I'll explain how helicopters work.

14
00:01:09.963 --> 00:01:11.863
My helicopter has two rotors.

15
00:01:13.404 --> 00:01:16.025
The main rotor sits on top of the helicopter.

16
00:01:17.886 --> 00:01:19.867
It spins really fast.

17
00:01:21.908 --> 00:01:23.869
I can control it with this lever.

18
00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:28.091
Two long wings are attached to the rotor.

19
00:01:29.391 --> 00:01:31.032
They're called rotor blades.

20
00:01:32.128 --> 00:01:34.510
When the rotor spins, the blades spin too.

21
00:01:36.912 --> 00:01:38.273
They push air down.

22
00:01:40.655 --> 00:01:42.437
That makes the helicopter go up.

23
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.462
I can also control the tilt of the rotor blades.

24
00:01:52.025 --> 00:01:55.788
By doing that, I can make the helicopter go in different directions.

25
00:01:59.808 --> 00:02:03.910
My helicopter's second rotor is attached to the helicopter's tail.

26
00:02:05.431 --> 00:02:08.172
It's smaller than the main one but just as important.

27
00:02:09.652 --> 00:02:10.233
Here's why.

28
00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:13.714
The main rotor blades spin in one direction.

29
00:02:15.115 --> 00:02:18.737
That makes the helicopter spin in the opposite direction.

30
00:02:22.198 --> 00:02:23.779
Nobody wants that to happen.

31
00:02:25.199 --> 00:02:26.320
We'd all get dizzy!

32
00:02:27.528 --> 00:02:29.989
So the tail rotor blades must spin too.

33
00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:35.791
That keeps the helicopter steady, stopping it from spinning out of control.

34
00:02:38.531 --> 00:02:41.692
Helicopters can't go as fast or as high as airplanes.

35
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:49.475
But they can go up and down, sideways and backward.

36
00:02:50.995 --> 00:02:53.236
They can also move slowly over the land.

37
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.841
This will help us spot the hurt hiker.

38
00:03:00.042 --> 00:03:01.443
Oh! There he is!

39
00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:05.666
Hmm. He's on a trail with a steep slope.

40
00:03:07.827 --> 00:03:10.548
I don't see anywhere safe for me to land my helicopter.

41
00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:13.810
But that's okay.

42
00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:14.811
I know what to do.

43
00:03:16.351 --> 00:03:20.814
Unlike planes, helicopters can stay up in the air, in one spot.

44
00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.096
I'll keep my helicopter right here.

45
00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:28.354
A rescue worker can go down to help the hiker.

46
00:03:30.636 --> 00:03:31.496
Good news!

47
00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:35.839
The rescue worker is back in the helicopter with the hiker.

48
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.081
Everyone is safe.

49
00:03:39.722 --> 00:03:41.063
Off we go to the hospital.

50
00:03:42.804 --> 00:03:43.605
We're almost there.

51
00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:47.167
Do you see that big circle with an H on the roof?

52
00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.470
I can gently land my helicopter on it.

53
00:03:53.772 --> 00:03:55.439
Well, my work is done.

54
00:03:57.223 --> 00:03:58.887
I'm heading back to the airport!
